{“question”: “Under the California CCPA, how much additional time may a company take to answer a complicated consumer request, and how soon must it notify the person of the delay?”, “answer”: “The business may extend the response period by up to 90 days in total when necessary. It must tell the consumer about the extension, with the reasons, within 45 days of receiving the request.”, “evidence”: [{“page”: 35, “quote”: “A time period for a business to respond to a consumer for any verifiable consumer request may be extended by up to a total of 90 days where necessary”}, {“page”: 35, “quote”: “The business shall inform the consumer of any such extension within 45 days of receipt of the request, together with the reasons for the delay.”}]}
